From 2947b89bf2be3d25eb0486266b443b440c12ba44 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daira-Emma Hopwood <daira@jacaranda.org>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 04:35:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] A 165-bit policy and a three-map compression chain, for
 planning

The single policy is the ADPS16-quantum gate at 165 bits, the level of
ML-KEM-768 and ML-DSA-65. The rank-one compression maps certify at
147.3 and 153.2 bits, so the chain becomes three maps with images of
2,304, 1,152, and 1,024 bits: rank 9 over a ring a quarter of the
terminal map's dimension, rank 9 over one an eighth of it, and rank 1
at the terminal dimension. The terminal payload stays 128 bytes.

This is for planning only. The parameters and the planner count a map's
relation rows and quotient rows by its rank. The rows of one map share a
family identity, the dispatch table has no arm for the small ring
dimensions, and the prover and the verifier are not adapted.

The compression cells hold the widths that an 8 KiB source needs. The
width tables are not regenerated here, only renamed for the policy: both
are to be regenerated at the floor, and the cells re-sized from them.

Tests of akita-params that fail at this commit: the dispatch arms for
the compression ladder; the witness tail's pinned length; and three that
pin table contents (two rank boundaries and the artifact digest).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Mythos 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
